
========================================================================================================
ROUTE B -- THE MEMORY-TIME ROUTE, TESTED. tau_mem = v_rel/a0 ?
========================================================================================================
  a0 = c H_Lambda / Z, Z = sqrt(32pi/3) = 5.78881  ->  a0 = 9.3600e-11 m/s^2 (canonical,
  pure-Lambda footing) = (c/2) sqrt(G rho_Lambda), i.e. EXACTLY HALF the free-fall
  acceleration at the dark-energy density. kappa = 1/2 is this framework's own coefficient
  and is not in the prior literature (Milgrom 1999 / Pikhitsa 2010 / Klinkhamer-Kopp 2011
  all give 2 c H_Lambda = 11.58x larger; Milgrom 2020 gives c H_Lambda/2pi). CAVEAT: 32pi/3
  is the Einstein-coupling conversion factor and CANCELS in that reduction -- the content
  is the ONE number kappa, which is FITTED, not derived.
  Alternate footing carried on every dimensional number: a0 = 1.1300e-10 m/s^2.
  c/a0 = 101.5 Gyr canonical, 84.1 Gyr alternate -- the
  frame-independent memory time Route B is trying to replace.

