========================================================================================================
  tau_mem = v/a0 ;  Omega tau_mem = Omega*v/a_0 ;  a/a0 = Omega*v/a_0
  [OK  ] Omega tau_mem - a/a0 = 0 identically in v, Omega and a0 on a circular orbit (sympy exact)
  [OK  ] and identically in R: v**2/(R*a_0) = v**2/(R*a_0) (no residual)
  [OK  ] Theorem 8 re-verified here: w/x = c/v exactly, kernel-free
  [OK  ] tau_mem = (v/c)(c/a0): Route B is EXACTLY the substitution c -> v_rel in the memory time, so it repairs Theorem 8's argument mismatch by construction on circles

