  THE RADIAL PATHOLOGY, quantified. Purely radial motion has v_t = 0.
    candidate A: Omega tau = A v_t/(v a0) -> 0 ;  candidate E: v_t v/(r a0) -> 0.
    Then Route B's law reads g_bar = |a| mu(0) = 0 for any FINITE |a|, so for g_bar > 0
    there is NO finite solution: the required acceleration DIVERGES. Exhibited by taking
    v_t -> 0 at fixed r and solving g_bar = A mu(A v_t/(v a0)) for A.
         v_t/v   A_required/a0 (alpha=2)   A_closure/a0      ratio
