  (iii) THE OSTROGRADSKY COST IS INHERITED, NOT AVOIDED. The only candidate that gives the
        closure off circles is B, whose argument is |xddot|/a0 -- literally the argument of
        the local witness action S = INT dt m(|xdot|^2 f(|xddot|/a0) - phi). So B is not a
        new theory; it is that action with a new interpretation, and it inherits the
        indefinite acceleration-Hessian. Re-verified here at 50 digits (mpmath), because
        this is a difference of large terms and a float64 scan reports thousands of
        SPURIOUS sign flips from an O(u^3) cancellation.
                 u          f2(u)       f2 prime      f2 second  f2p/u (transv.)  indefinite?
