  [OK  ] at 50-digit precision the alpha=2 generating function has f'' < 0 (longitudinal) and f'/u > 0 (transverse) at every u over 10 decades: the acceleration-Hessian is INDEFINITE, so omega_extra^2 < 0 and the extra modes are runaways. Candidate B inherits this in full (0.57 s e-folding at Earth, 5e7 yr at 30 kpc, |omega|/Omega_orb = 2.8 per the corpus)
  [OK  ] Newtonian limit intact for both kernels, f(inf) = 1/2 (f2 = 0.500000000, f1 = 0.499999995) -- the control that says the generating functions are the right objects

  ITEM 4 VERDICT. ESTABLISHED: (1) the corpus's Herglotz/passivity chain does not transfer
  to a state-dependent corner, and the reason is structural (linearity is used, not
  incidental); (2) both kernels are strictly concave on z > 0, so the function-vs-average
  gap is POSITIVE-DEFINITE off circles and vanishes only for single-frequency trajectories;
  (3) the gap on an e=0.6 galaxy orbit is order 1-10%, and Route B does not reduce it;
  (4) the one candidate that reproduces the closure lands back on the local witness action
  and its runaway modes. NOT ESTABLISHED, and not claimed: whether some nonlinear-passivity
  notion (e.g. a state-dependent KMS/fluctuation-dissipation condition) could rescue
  positivity. That is a real open question and this script does not settle it.

========================================================================================================
S7. ONE FALSIFIABLE CONSEQUENCE, and it lands on the FROZEN pre-registration
========================================================================================================
  Route B's drag level is not a philosophical choice -- it changes the wide-binary
  prediction by orders of magnitude, which is Front A (Gaia DR4, ~Dec 2026).
       sep   u = a/a0      v_int  v_gal/v_int  arg (barycentre)  arg (galactoc.)   mu_bary    mu_gal
        2k    15.8744     666.8m/s          330           15.8744           5237.9   0.99802  1.000000
        5k     2.7028     435.0m/s          506            2.7028           1366.9   0.93787  1.000000
       10k     0.9304     360.9m/s          610            0.9304            567.1   0.68115  0.999998
       20k     0.4141     340.5m/s          646            0.4141            267.5   0.38259  0.999993
       30k     0.2701     336.8m/s          653            0.2701            176.4   0.26073  0.999984
  [OK  ] in the 10-30 kAU band the two drag levels are DIFFERENT THEORIES: galactocentric gives mu = 0.999984-0.999998 (pure Newton, gamma -> 1) while barycentre-dragged gives mu = 0.2607-0.6812 (a 74% boost). The argument jumps by v_gal/v_int = 610-653x. So Route B REPRODUCES the corpus's wide-binary DC-vs-AC gate fork under a new name -- it does not resolve it. The frozen DR4 target gamma = 1.0246 (MI) belongs to the barycentre-dragged branch only; the galactocentric branch predicts gamma = 1
  [OK  ] and the fork is SEPARATION-DEPENDENT, which is why it is testable rather than a redefinition: at 2 kAU both branches are Newtonian (mu ratio 1.0020), so the two drag levels only separate where u < 1
  NOTE ON PROCESS: PREREGISTRATION_DR4.md is FROZEN and hash-stamped. Nothing here changes
  a frozen target; this is a statement about which BRANCH the frozen target belongs to, and
  if Route B were ever adopted it would need an amendment filed IN THE OPEN before DR4.

========================================================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================================================
  Route B is PARTIAL, and the partition is sharp.
  WHAT WORKS, exactly and on both footings: on a circular orbit tau_mem = v_rel/a0 delivers
    Omega tau_mem = a/a0 identically, which is precisely the argument Theorem 8 found
    missing, and the enumeration shows c CANNOT appear in tau_mem -- so 'the frame must be
    locally dragged' is FORCED, not chosen. That is a genuine, if narrow, gain.
  WHAT DOES NOT WORK.
    * It pins nothing. The circular identity leaves a one-parameter monomial family and an
      infinite-dimensional function family; omega_c is not measured, it is replaced by a
      rule that is itself free off circles.
    * The drag level is triple-locked into an impossible corner: cosmic frame excluded by
      1.00 dex vs a 0.216 dex budget; local-matter drag excluded by 3.6-11x mis-scaling
      of a0 per disk population; and the barycentre prescription that survives both is
      NOT expressible as a local field, because two co-located stars in nested systems
      need frames differing by 8-25x in speed.
    * Off circles no candidate frequency survives: B is a tautology that lands back inside
      corrected Theorem 3, A and E diverge on radial motion, G is unboundedly wrong there.
    * The gap Theorem 8 names is K(<Box_u>) != <K(Box_u)>, and that is a function-vs-average
      statement. Both kernels are strictly concave, so the gap is positive-definite off
      circles by Jensen and is untouched by any rescaling of the argument. Route B repairs
      the argument and leaves the inequality exactly where it was.
  NOVELTY, assessed not asserted: the identity Omega (v/a0) = a/a0 is elementary kinematics;
  inertia-relative-to-matter is Mach (Sciama 1953 for the standard citation); orbit-dependent
  interpolating functions in modified inertia are Milgrom 1994 Ann.Phys. 229:384; and the
  single-frequency restriction is Milgrom 2022 PRD 106:064060. What is not in that prior art,
  as far as this script can tell, is the THREE-WAY DRAG LOCK of S4 and the Jensen signing of
  S6 -- both of which are NEGATIVE results about this framework, not new physics.
  NO DOOR IS DECLARED CLOSED. The unsettled piece is named in S6: whether a state-dependent
  passivity/KMS condition exists at all.
========================================================================================================
